#: includes/admin.php:234 includes/admin.php:685
msgid "WP Masking"
msgstr "WP Masking"

#: includes/admin.php:235
msgid ""
"Hides the WordPress structure in the pages visitors receive. The web server "
"maps the new paths back to the real files; the rules are part of tegatai-"
"nginx.conf (nginx) or of the Tegatai block in .htaccess (Apache, LiteSpeed)."
msgstr ""
"Hides the WordPress structure in the pages visitors receive. The web server "
"maps the new paths back to the real files; the rules are part of tegatai-"
"nginx.conf (nginx) or of the Tegatai block in .htaccess (Apache, LiteSpeed)."

#: includes/admin.php:239
msgid "Hide plugin and theme paths"
msgstr "Hide plugin and theme paths"

#: includes/admin.php:239
msgid ""
"Plugin and theme folders are shown under their own names, e.g. /assets/bar/ "
"instead of the plugin folder."
msgstr ""
"Plugin and theme folders are shown under their own names, e.g. /assets/bar/ "
"instead of the plugin folder."

#: includes/admin.php:240
msgid "Hide wp-includes, wp-json and admin-ajax"
msgstr "Hide wp-includes, wp-json and admin-ajax"

#: includes/admin.php:240
msgid ""
"wp-includes, the REST API and admin-ajax.php get their own paths. /wp-json/ "
"keeps working for The Hive and other sites."
msgstr ""
"wp-includes, the REST API and admin-ajax.php get their own paths. /wp-json/ "
"keeps working for The Hive and other sites."

#: includes/admin.php:241
msgid "Remove versions and identifiers"
msgstr "Remove versions and identifiers"

#: includes/admin.php:241
msgid ""
"Removes ?ver= parameters, script/style ids, generator tags, "
"RSD/wlwmanifest/shortlink/REST links, the emoji script, the speculation "
"rules (they list the WordPress paths) and the X-Pingback header."
msgstr ""
"Removes ?ver= parameters, script/style ids, generator tags, "
"RSD/wlwmanifest/shortlink/REST links, the emoji script, the speculation "
"rules (they list the WordPress paths) and the X-Pingback header."

#: includes/admin.php:242
msgid "Hide file names"
msgstr "Hide file names"

#: includes/admin.php:242
msgid ""
"File names of masked plugin, theme and wp-includes files are replaced by a "
"neutral name per file, e.g. /assets/bar/css/t3f9a0c1d2e4. The folders stay, "
"so relative URLs in CSS and JS keep working. A changed file gets a new name."
msgstr ""
"File names of masked plugin, theme and wp-includes files are replaced by a "
"neutral name per file, e.g. /assets/bar/css/t3f9a0c1d2e4. The folders stay, "
"so relative URLs in CSS and JS keep working. A changed file gets a new name."

#. translators: 1: number of active file names, 2: number of waiting file
#. names
#: includes/admin.php:247
#, php-format
msgid "File names: %1$d active, %2$d waiting."
msgstr "File names: %1$d active, %2$d waiting."

#: includes/admin.php:248
msgid ""
"New files are found when pages are visited. Tegatai adds them to the rules "
"and checks them every hour; they are used as soon as the web server knows "
"the rules (nginx: after a reload; Apache and LiteSpeed: at once). \"Check "
"new paths\" does both right away."
msgstr ""
"New files are found when pages are visited. Tegatai adds them to the rules "
"and checks them every hour; they are used as soon as the web server knows "
"the rules (nginx: after a reload; Apache and LiteSpeed: at once). \"Check "
"new paths\" does both right away."

#: includes/admin.php:251
msgid "Block original paths"
msgstr "Block original paths"

#: includes/admin.php:251
msgid ""
"Visitors get a 404 for the original paths of masked entries. Logged-in users"
" keep access. /wp-json/tegatai/ (The Hive) stays reachable."
msgstr ""
"Visitors get a 404 for the original paths of masked entries. Logged-in users"
" keep access. /wp-json/tegatai/ (The Hive) stays reachable."

#: includes/admin.php:254
msgid "How it is activated"
msgstr "How it is activated"

#: includes/admin.php:255
msgid ""
"1. Switch on and save the names. 2. nginx: reload nginx so the new rules are"
" active (Apache and LiteSpeed read the .htaccess at once). 3. Click \"Check "
"new paths\". Only paths that answered correctly are used in the pages and "
"blocked, so a missing reload never breaks the site."
msgstr ""
"1. Switch on and save the names. 2. nginx: reload nginx so the new rules are"
" active (Apache and LiteSpeed read the .htaccess at once). 3. Click \"Check "
"new paths\". Only paths that answered correctly are used in the pages and "
"blocked, so a missing reload never breaks the site."

